📄 Page 1: JiraFlowCoordinator
🎯 Purpose

JiraFlowCoordinator is the main orchestrator of the Jira integration flow.

It is the class that coordinates the complete process from the moment the integration starts until the execution is published into Jira. It does not perform all tasks itself. Instead, it:

• stores the main configuration
• resolves the execution context
• prepares the data needed by the other classes
• decides the high-level execution order
• delegates responsibilities to the gateway, Test Plan manager, report builder, and execution publisher

This class is the entry point of the integration.

🧠 Why this class exists

The integration involves multiple independent concerns:

• resolving the correct Katalon report folder
• identifying the current suite name
• locating the XML execution result
• generating the custom GAIA HTML report
• resolving or creating a Jira Test Plan
• importing results and publishing attachments

Without a central coordinator, these responsibilities would be scattered and much harder to maintain.

JiraFlowCoordinator centralizes the flow control and ensures every step happens in the correct order.

🏗️ Position in the architecture

This class sits at the top of the integration flow.

It instantiates and coordinates:

• JiraGateway
• JiraTestPlanManager
• JiraGaiaReportBuilder
• JiraExecutionPublisher

Direct dependencies

• RunConfiguration from Katalon
• Apache POI for reading LastRun.xlsx
• local filesystem under the project Reports folder
• helper methods inside the same class

Classes it creates

• new JiraGateway(this)
• new JiraTestPlanManager(this, gateway)
• new JiraGaiaReportBuilder(this)
• new JiraExecutionPublisher(this, gateway)

🔗 Integrations
Katalon integration

This class depends on Katalon runtime information, mainly:

• RunConfiguration.projectDir
• RunConfiguration.getReportFolder()

These are used to detect the current project and the report location.

Filesystem integration

This class reads and resolves:

• Reports folder
• LastRun.xlsx
• XML report files
• image evidence files
• local TestPlanKeys folder

Jira integration

This class does not call Jira endpoints directly.

Instead, it delegates Jira communication to JiraGateway.

Report generation integration

This class triggers GAIA report creation through JiraGaiaReportBuilder.

