📄 Page 2: JiraGateway
🎯 Purpose

JiraGateway is the Jira communication layer of the integration.

It is the class responsible for sending requests to Jira, reading responses, validating status codes, and converting response bodies into structured values that the rest of the integration can use.

This class acts as the boundary between Katalon and Jira.

🧠 Why this class exists

Without a gateway layer, Jira request logic would be spread across multiple classes. That would make it much harder to:

• reuse API logic
• validate responses consistently
• isolate Jira-specific technical behavior
• debug request failures
• change request objects or endpoint structure later

This class centralizes all Jira communication.

🏗️ Position in the architecture

JiraGateway is a service class used by:

• JiraFlowCoordinator indirectly
• JiraTestPlanManager
• JiraExecutionPublisher

It does not decide high-level flow. It only performs Jira operations requested by other classes.

🔗 Integrations
