🔍 findExistingTestPlanKey(String summary)
Purpose

Attempts to resolve an already existing Test Plan key without creating a new one.

Resolution order
1. Force new Test Plan

If FORCE_CREATE_NEW_TEST_PLAN is true, the method immediately returns blank and skips all reuse logic.

Why

This intentionally forces the creation path.

2. Manual Test Plan key

If MANUAL_TEST_PLAN_KEY is filled, it is returned immediately.

Why

This is an explicit override and has priority over all automatic logic.

3. Saved local Test Plan key

The method reads the suite-specific saved key from disk.

If a saved key exists, it validates the Jira issue by calling:

gateway.getIssueByKey(savedKey)

Then it checks:

• summary must match the expected summary
• issue type must be Test Plan

Why

This prevents reuse of a stale or wrong key.

Important behavior

If validation fails, the saved key is ignored and the method continues.

4. Search Jira for existing Test Plans

Calls:

gateway.searchTestPlans(summary, owner.EPIC_KEY)

Then filters the returned issues by exact normalized summary match.

Important detail

Exact matching is done here, not inside the gateway.

Selection logic

If multiple exact matches exist:

• the newest one is used
• the chosen key is saved locally

Why

This avoids creating duplicates when a matching Test Plan already exists.

Return values

• existing Test Plan key
• blank if none found
• ERROR_* if search failed

🆕 getOrCreateTestPlanKey()
Purpose

Returns a valid Test Plan key for the current suite, creating one when needed.

Flow

builds the expected summary using owner.getTestPlanName()

tries findExistingTestPlanKey(summary)

if an error is returned, propagates the error

if an existing key is found, returns it

otherwise calls gateway.createTestPlan(summary, owner.EPIC_KEY)

saves the created key locally if successful

Why it matters

This is the final public entry point used by the main flow.

💾 Local persistence behavior

This class uses the filesystem through the coordinator to store suite-to-TestPlan mappings.

Benefit

Reduces unnecessary Jira searches and keeps suite resolution faster.

Risk

If the saved key is stale and validation logic is too weak, the wrong Test Plan could be reused.

📝 What each decision means
FORCE_CREATE_NEW_TEST_PLAN

Disables reuse completely.

MANUAL_TEST_PLAN_KEY

Uses one explicit Jira Test Plan key.

Saved key validation

Optimizes reuse while still checking correctness.

Exact title match

Prevents accidental reuse of similarly named Test Plans.

