📄 Page: JiraGaiaHtmlTemplateBuilder
Overview

JiraGaiaHtmlTemplateBuilder is the class responsible for generating the final HTML structure of the GAIA report. It receives a normalized model containing suite information, scenarios, steps, status, timing, and evidence, and converts that model into a complete self-contained HTML page with embedded CSS and JavaScript. In practice, this class is the presentation layer of the GAIA report, while JiraGaiaReportBuilder is the data preparation layer.

Purpose in the integration

The goal of this class is to transform execution data into a readable and interactive report that can be opened locally and attached to Jira. Instead of exposing raw XML, raw logs, or unstructured evidence, it organizes everything into a visual report with a sidebar, searchable scenarios, scenario detail panels, evidence previews, and execution charts. This makes failures easier to analyze and helps the team inspect the execution directly from the generated HTML artifact.

Called by

JiraGaiaReportBuilder.createGaiaHtmlReport()

Main responsibility

This class is responsible for the final rendering of the GAIA report. It does not parse Jira responses, does not call endpoints, and does not read XML directly. Its only job is to take already prepared execution data and render it into HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

What this class builds

The generated report includes:

• the HTML document structure
• the report title and top banner
• the GAIA logo reference
• the sidebar with Tests and Charts tabs
• the searchable scenario list
• the scenario detail panels
• the steps table for each scenario
• the visual error section for failed scenarios
• the evidence preview block
• the global chart overview
• all embedded CSS styling
• all embedded JavaScript interactions

Position in the architecture

This class belongs to the report visualization layer.

Input

It receives a Map model from JiraGaiaReportBuilder.

Output

It returns a single HTML string.

Related classes

• JiraGaiaReportBuilder prepares the report model
• JiraGaiaHtmlTemplateBuilder renders the final HTML page

