JiraFlowCoordinator.getTestPlanName()

The Epic value comes from:

JiraFlowCoordinator.EPIC_KEY

Expected response

On success, Jira returns a JSON body containing the created issue key. The integration reads:

• key

That value becomes the resolved Test Plan key.

Success criteria

The current implementation accepts:

• 200
• 201

Failure behavior

If the response status is not accepted, the method returns:

ERROR<statusCode>

The main flow then stops because the execution cannot be published without a resolved Test Plan.

Why this endpoint is important

This endpoint is the fallback creation mechanism for Test Plans. It ensures the integration can still complete even when no reusable Test Plan exists yet in Jira.

Common maintenance scenarios

Update this endpoint page when:

• the Epic custom field ID changes
• additional Jira fields must be filled during creation
• the issue type changes
• project mapping changes
• Test Plan creation needs more metadata such as labels or components

Risks and attention points

Be careful with:

• customfield_10006 because it is environment-specific
• Jira issue type name Test Plan
• summary naming consistency
• project key correctness
• hardcoded request URL in the saved request object

